<p><strong>A business captures after-hours bookings when customers can see free slots and book themselves at any time, rather than waiting for someone to answer the phone the next morning.</strong></p>
@<p><em>The scene below is a typical one, not a single named customer.</em></p>
<h2>The 11 pm decision</h2>
<p>Someone is scrolling at home and decides to book a massage for the weekend. They call, but it is closed. They send a message and do not hear back until the next day. By then, they have booked somewhere else.</p>
<h2>Why it happens</h2>
<ul><li>Booking only works while staff are at the desk.</li><li>Messages sit unanswered overnight.</li><li>Tourists and busy professionals decide outside opening hours.</li></ul>
<h2>How it is solved</h2>
<p>With <a href="/features/booking/">online booking</a>, customers choose the branch, service, staff member and a free slot at any hour, from their phone. The booking goes straight into the shared schedule, so it cannot clash with phone or walk-in bookings. Read the <a href="/blog/online-booking-system-nepal/">online booking system guide</a>.</p>
<h2>A quick fix you can start today</h2>
<ol><li>Put one booking link on your Google profile, Instagram and WhatsApp status.</li><li>Show only free slots so customers cannot ask for taken ones.</li><li>Check the new bookings first thing each morning.</li></ol>
<p>Also see <a href="/blog/spa-booking-app-nepal/">how spas can take bookings from tourists</a>, or <a href="#try-free" data-trial-open>try the free Zennly demo</a>.</p>
